<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">The retirement of the MinTLS =3D 0 (=A1=B0None=A1=B1) configuratio=
n option is part of the broader TLS 1.0/1.1 retirement effort across Azure,=
 which was announced to customers approximately two
 years ago. Azure established TLS 1.2 as the minimum required version for c=
lient connections as part of that initiative, and customers were notified t=
hrough Azure-wide and Azure database=A8Cspecific communications.</span><spa=
n lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">&nbsp;</span><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">Since then, we have been gradually phasing out the MinTLS =3D 0 se=
tting, as it enables negotiation of legacy TLS versions that are no longer =
supported. In most cases, this configuration
 has already become obsolete, especially for customers whose clients are al=
ready using TLS 1.2 or higher, including those who migrated.</span><span la=
ng=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">&nbsp;</span><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">The current communication targets the final retirement of the conf=
iguration option itself, rather than introducing a new requirement. While t=
he affected population is relatively small
 (customers using unencrypted connections), these customers were included i=
n the original broad TLS 1.2 requirement announcements. However, they were =
not explicitly segmented in prior reminder communications, which is why thi=
s targeted notification is being
 issued now.</span><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">&nbsp;</span><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"xmsonormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;colo=
r:black">Given that this is the final enforcement step in an already shared=
, multi-phase TLS retirement effort, we did not treat this as a new, standa=
lone 12-month retirement notice, but rather
 as a follow-up action to complete the previously announced requirement.</s=
pan><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
